  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Atlas Air obligated $565M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Atlas Air received 339 awards so far, with an average award size of $1.7M. Atlas Air obligations are down 25.6% year over year. Atlas Air has shown large swings across fiscal years: FY21 obligations were $13.5M, FY22 obligations were $1.7M, FY23 obligations were $6M, FY24 obligations were $3.7M, and FY25 obligations were $759M. Atlas Air revenue in FY2026 is concentrated in air-transport markets. Atlas Air obligated $563M in Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation and $1.1M in Scheduled Freight Air Transportation. Atlas Air has smaller obligations in related services: $333K in Other Technical and Trade Schools and $332K in Flight Training. Atlas Air current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing, and award-value figures in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than current-year obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did Atlas Air obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Atlas Air obligations fell 25.6% year over year. Atlas Air saw much higher obligations in FY25 at $759M compared with $565M in FY26 to date, which shows the current year is lower than the prior fiscal year total. Atlas Air prior-year variability is visible across FY21–FY25, with values ranging from $1.7M to $759M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is Atlas Air concentrated by market?",
        "body": "Atlas Air is concentrated in Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation with $563M obligated in FY2026 to date. Atlas Air also has obligations in Scheduled Freight Air Transportation at $1.1M, and in training and education services: Other Technical and Trade Schools at $333K and Flight Training at $332K."
      }
    ]
